{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/623","id":5054724834,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-xXos8AAAABLUj64g","html_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/623","diff_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/623.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/mw00/project-maya/pull/623.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/623","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/623/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/623/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/issues/623/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mw00/project-maya/statuses/b772203a4acfd7e88f7476fc7a6f33359b26f549","number":623,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"CPU lane: IQ1_M rows with folded scales and int16 sums, IQ2_XS one-token own rows (bit for bit ggml-cpu dot)","user":{"login":"SeriousRising","id":69419008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDE5MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69419008?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising","html_url":"https://github.com/SeriousRising","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SeriousRising/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**What.** `src/kernels/cpu/iq_avx2.cpp` (`row_dot_iq1m`, `row_dot_iq2xs`, `iq256_rows1_supported`), on top of #452's rows:\n\n- **IQ1_M.** A microbenchmark showed #452's rows are bound by the total uop count (Broadwell: 4 a cycle, ~20 cycles per 64 weights), not by the shuffle port. Two exact integer identities cut the uops:\n  1. IQ1_M grid bytes are only -1 / 0 / +1, so `maddubs(|g|, sign(q8, g))` equals `maddubs(scale, sign(q8, g))` with the block scale folded in, and both `|g|` sign ops go.\n  2. Scales 2s + 1 <= 15 go into maddubs' unsigned operand. A lane is at most 2 x 15 x 128 = 3840, and 8 of them a block at most 30720, which fits int16. So the sums accumulate in int16, with **one `madd` a block** instead of 4 `madd` + 4 `add` per 64 weights.\n\n  Grid indices come from ggml's `pdep` form where `pdep` is fast (CPUID: BMI2, and not AMD / Hygon below family 19h), elsewhere from scalar indices into a 4-entry table. The delta signs come from one broadcast of qh, with no `set_epi64x`. The int32 lanes per block are ggml's exact integers, and ggml's float steps are unchanged.\n- **IQ2_XS.** The grid by `tab4` from scalar u16 loads, half-scales from a 256-entry table. Its one-token own rows are enabled (type 17 in `iq256_rows1_supported` / `iq256_rows1`); before, IQ2_XS at one token fell back to ggml's `vec_dot`.\n- No AVX2 code runs before `main`: the tables are `constexpr` (`.rodata`), and the `pdep` probe is a function-local static behind `cpu_avx2_ok()`, so a pre-AVX2 CPU still reaches the ggml fallback.\n- Tests: `native_rows_exact_test` gains the IQ1_M int16 worst case (every scale 15, an all +1 grid, every delta bit, q8 = -127, lanes at +-30480). `ds4_lane_bench` gains an `iq2_xs` format and prints the exactness of each format's one-token and multi-token rows.\n\n**Setting:** `DS4_IQ1M_PDEP=0/1` forces the index form on a BMI2 CPU, for checking the other form (both exact); unset = the CPUID choice above. A row in `docs/SETTINGS.md`, beside `DS4_IQ1_PDEP`.\n\n**Overlap with #584** (open): #584 sends one-token IQ1_M rows to ggml-cpu's own BMI2 dot where `pdep` is fast. This PR touches the same routing: our rows are faster than ggml's dot at one token (table below) and also cover several tokens, which #584 leaves alone. If #584 lands first, this replaces its one-token routing with these rows and would keep its `cpu_pdep_slow()` probe instead of ours; happy to rebase either way.\n\n| IQ1_M, one 2304 x 5120 matrix, one Broadwell core, L3-resident | ms |\n|---|---|\n| #452's rows (v1.1.35) | 2.292 |\n| ggml-cpu AVX2 + BMI2 dot (what #584 routes to) | 1.269 |\n| this PR, `pdep`-free form (chosen on Zen 1/2, Hygon) | 1.402 |\n| **this PR, `pdep` form** | **1.152** |\n\n**Output: unchanged**, bit for bit ggml-cpu's dot:\n\n- the engine's start gate is unchanged (`rows_match_ggml`: 306 one-token rows and nt 2/5/11, with the subnormal shifts; any mismatch falls back to ggml); both forms pass it for IQ1_M and IQ2_XS;\n- `native_rows_exact_test`: \"all identical\" with `DS4_IQ1M_PDEP` unset, `=0` and `=1`;\n- `ds4_iq1_rows_test` (`DS4_IQ1_PDEP=0` and `=1`, its two CMake tests): 36 cases, 0 differ from ggml-cpu's dot;\n- `ds4_lane_bench --check`: IQ1_M and IQ2_XS own rows bit-identical to ggml's dot, one token and several; every format within 1.8e-7 of the double reference;\n- `ds4_gguf_test`: ALL OK; the engine run below gives the same token ids and DSpark counts as v1.1.35.\n\n**Measured.** CPU: 16-vCPU Xeon E5-2697 v4 VM (Broadwell, AVX2 + BMI2, 4-channel DDR4-2133), g++ 13.3, `-march=native`. `ds4_lane_bench`, one token, an expert end to end (gate/up/down, activation quant, SiLU, the pool's jobs), v1.1.35's binary vs this branch's, one run each:\n\n| format | 1 thread, v1.1.35 | 1 thread, this PR | 14 threads, v1.1.35 | 14 threads, this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| IQ1_M | 7.097 ms | **4.199** (1.69x) | 0.757 | **0.387** (1.96x) |\n| IQ2_XS | (no `iq2_xs` format in v1.1.35's bench) | 3.522 | | 0.338 |\n| IQ2_XXS (code unchanged) | 4.423 | 4.811 | 0.489 | 0.498 |\n\n(IQ2_XXS's code is not changed; its 1-thread difference is run-to-run spread on a shared VM.)\n\nEngine: 2x CMP 170HX 64 GB (sm_80; PCIe Gen2 x16 + Gen2 x4, platform-specific), DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017 GSQ-RCO IQ2_XXS (routed experts IQ1_M / IQ2_XS / IQ2_XXS; most in VRAM, the rest on the CPU lane), `--tp 1 --gpus 0,1 --dspark on --cpu-threads 14 --suffix-draft 0`, 2000 fixed prompt ids + 256 greedy tokens, one run per binary: verify time 5086.6 -> 4529.6 ms over the same 80 DSpark rounds (**-11 %**), decode 40.68 -> 45.10 tok/s, the same ids. Earlier, through the server on our v1.1.29-based fork (5 prompts x 512 tokens, temperature 0): -6.5 % / -3.8 % a verify window, `--dspark none` -3.1 % / -2.3 % a step, the same text; the larger gain on v1.1.35 was not analysed.\n\nZen 3 / Zen 4 / newer Intel (the `pdep` form) and Zen 1/2 / Hygon (the `pdep`-free form): not measured. The gain depends on how much CPU-lane time is exposed; a box that streams more experts from RAM should gain more (not measured).\n\n**Checks** (as `.github/workflows/tests.yml`): `tools/check_hip_compat.py` OK; server tests 463 OK (12 skipped); installer and tools tests 584 OK (31 skipped) - the same counts as v1.1.35.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-28T17:20:46Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T08:38:09Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T08:38:09Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"200491df9719b15cf02245012c05c9261ae5c04c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SeriousRising:cpu-iq1m-iq2xs-rows","ref":"cpu-iq1m-iq2xs-rows","repo":{"id":1437354424,"node_id":"R_kgDOVaxJuA","name":"project-maya","full_name":"SeriousRising/project-maya","owner":{"login":"SeriousRising","id":69419008,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5NDE5MDA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69419008?v=4","gravatar_